b5-3a64-42d9/62eb-5e6f-512a-420d/6850-af5c-a4a1-4c5d/70f5-2253-1671-474d/91b0-6185-b53c-4271/a516-e61b-ede9-465c/a691-f454-92c5-49bd/cacb-8d57-efff-4ab1/ce8f-4da9-2836-4115/e755-9371-7951-454a/fd6b-09c5-8f76-45ad"],"finding":"Child 0d3c (F13) says the fix is 'One line each' for code-review and completion-verification, directly contradicting the parent plan's explicit instruction that this is NOT one line each — the parent mandates each gate get its OWN required-step-id frozenset DERIVED from that gate's dispatcher references plus a sited call. A child that ships only two one-line calls reusing plan-review's set makes the check pass vacuously, exactly the failure the parent warns against.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb5dced6d728a9f02","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 0d3c-ff25-5317-4d73","norm_id":"n85b27baa0916c132","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer follows the child's 'one line each' and calls _validate_gate_step_ids with _PLAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED_STEP_IDS for code-review; the check passes vacuously and a verify/decide rename still degrades the run silently — the exact defect the child exists to prevent."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Amend the child to specify: introduce _CODE_REVIEW_REQUIRED_STEP_IDS and a completion-verification frozenset, each derived from that gate's actual dispatcher step references, and add a _validate_gate_step_ids call after each gate's _gate_doc load.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact